{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>And it was set before him to eat.</b> ויושם is the reading (qeri); ויישם is the written form (ketiv), with two yods. And our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: he cast poison of death into the bowl so that he would die and take all his wealth, but it did not succeed in their hands, for it became mixed up with Bethuel's portion. Therefore it is written ויישם, for the letter vav and the two yods equal the numerical value of the Name. And the verse hints to you that he would have eaten the poison were it not for the HaShem that was with him, Who saved him in the merit of Abraham, and he did not eat until he had spoken all his words. And at the end of the matters it mentions: ״ויאכלו וישתו הוא והאנשים אשר עמו״ — to exclude the members of the household, who did not eat, for they were mourning over Bethuel, who died by means of the poison; for the servant was saved in the merit of Abraham, and the wicked one came in his stead — and this is why it is written ״ויאמר אחיה ואמה״, and it does not mention her father."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:14:48.559627843Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}